JLAB 250MHz Flash ADC Board Library - Moller Implementation
------------------------------------------------------------

   The JLAB FADC Library has been extended to support Hall A Moller
polarimeter triggering and processing. The FADC generates internal triggers
based on the 16 inputs. It is a single FADC design.

   The Moller library extensions are included in the file mollerLib.c. This
file is included in the standard library fadcLib.c and all files must be available to 
build the Moller based library. One must define INCLUDE_MOLLER to build Moller extensions.
See the example Makefile in the distribution.

  The JLAB FADC trigger FPGA can be programmed via a a set of VME accessable 
registers to define the internal triggering. The following library functions can be
used to progam these registers:

   int famSetSumThresh(int det, unsigned int lr, unsigned int val);

Set the Left or Right side Sum threshhold for the calorimeter trigger
    det = 0
    lr  = 0 or 1
    val = 0 - 0xfffff

   int famSetSampleCount(int det, unsigned int lr, unsigned int val);

Set the number of samples to sum from Left or Right side calorimeter signals
    det = 0
    lr  = 0 or 1
    val = 3 - 63

   int famSetPrescale(int det, unsigned int lr, unsigned int val);

Set the Trigger Prescale factor for each of the three internal trigger types (CL, CR, CL*CR)
    det = 0
    lr  = 0 or 1 or 2
    val = 1 - 2047

   int famSetPulseWidth(int det, unsigned int lr, unsigned int val);

Set the Pulse Width (in clock ticks - 4ns/tick) for signal inputs
    det = 0,1,2,3,4
    lr  = 0 or 1
    val = 3 - 255     

   int famSetDelay(int det, unsigned int lr, unsigned int val);

Set the Delay (in clock ticks) for the signal inputs (and Scint coincidence)

    det = 0,1,2,3,4,5
    lr  = 0 or 1
    val = 0 - 255   (4ns - 1024ns)

   int famSetTrigWindow(unsigned int val);

Set the Trigger coincidence window (in clock ticks) for each of the 3 trigger types

    det = 0
    lr  = 0 or 1 or 2
    val = 0 - 255   (4ns - 1024ns)


The parameters are:

     det =   0   Calorimeter
             1   Scint 1
             2   Scint 2
             3   Scint 3
             4   Scint 4
             5   ScintLeft * ScintRight

     lr =    0   (Left)
             1   (Right)
             2   (Left * Right)


Programming status of all the available registers can be seen with the following print
command:

-> faMollerStatus

STATUS for MOLLER FADC in slot 5 at base address 0x90ed0000 
---------------------------------------------------------- 
Moller FPGA Firmware Rev/ID = 0x0801 
Note: All values are in clock ticks (4ns/tick)

                         Left               Right
Sample Count                 3                    3    
Sum Threshold              255                  255    
Pulse Widths:
   Calorimeter               3                    3     
   Scint 1                   3                    3     
   Scint 2                   3                    3     
   Scint 3                   3                    3     
   Scint 4                   3                    3     
Delays     :
   Calorimeter               0                    0     
   Scint 1                   0                    0     
   Scint 2                   0                    0     
   Scint 3                   0                    0     
   Scint 4                   0                    0     
   SL*SR   :        0
Cal Trigger Prescales:
   Left: 1    Right: 1   CR*CL: 1
value = 0 = 0x0
-> 

